{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5391) from a cobbler code generation pipeline. The task requires implementing `cmd/cp` for the go-unix-utils project, specifically covering only srd056-cp requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (basic file copying). Two files must be created: `cmd/cp/main.go` (implementation) and `cmd/cp/cp_test.go` (differential tests). The implementation must follow strict project conventions including copyright headers, SIGPIPE handling, differential testing against GNU `gcp`, and function/file size limits.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: Compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gcp`) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: All cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **srd056-cp R1.1-R1.4 requirements**:\n     - R1.1: Basic `cp SOURCE DEST` and multi-file `cp SOURCE... DEST_DIR` copy\n     - R1.2: `-i`/`--interactive` prompts before overwriting existing files\n     - R1.3: `-f`/`--force` removes destination if can't open, retries copy\n     - R1.4: `-n`/`--no-clobber` silently skips existing destinations; `-n` takes precedence over `-i`\n   - **Non-goals** (must NOT implement): `--reflink`, `--sparse`, `-u`, `--backup`, SELinux context\n   - **Scope boundary**: Must NOT implement R2 (recursive/symlinks), R3 (attribute preservation), or R4.3/R4.4 (target-directory, full differential test suite) — only R1.1-R1.4\n   - **Go module**: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - **Build command**: `go build -o bin/cp ./cmd/cp/`\n   - **No git commands**: Git is managed externally by the orchestrator\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd056-cp.yaml** (READ)\n     - Contains full SRD for cp utility with R1-R4 requirement groups\n     - R1 (Basic file copying): R1.1 (copy semantics), R1.2 (interactive), R1.3 (force), R1.4 (no-clobber)\n     - R2 (Recursive/symlinks): NOT in scope for this task\n     - R3 (Attribute preservation): NOT in scope for this task  \n     - R4 (Exit codes/testing): R4.1-R4.2 exit codes are relevant but R4.3-R4.4 are NOT in scope\n     - Non-goals: --reflink, --sparse, -u, --backup, SELinux context\n   \n   - **cmd/cp/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Must implement basic file copying with -i, -f, -n flags\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start\n     - Must include SPDX copyright header\n     - Functions must not exceed 40 lines\n   \n   - **cmd/cp/cp_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Must use differential testing pattern with `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gcp\")`\n     - Must skip gracefully if `gcp` not in PATH\n     - Must cover R1.1-R1.4 behaviors\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - Key exports: `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests`, `BuildBinary`, `NormalizeFunc`, `ComposeNormalizers`\n     - `DiffTest` struct has fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte` enables checking file system state after copy\n\n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` installs SIGPIPE handler for clean exit on broken pipe\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/build.go** (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the cmd/ package and returns binary path\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full cp specification and identify which requirements are in scope (R1.1-R1.4 only)\n   - Identified that cp for this task should handle: single file copy, multi-file copy into directory, interactive mode (-i), force mode (-f), no-clobber mode (-n), and the precedence rule (-n over -i)\n   - Need to handle exit codes: 0 on success, 1 on failure (R4.1, R4.2 are implicitly needed)\n   - The `ExpectedFiles` field on `DiffTest` struct allows verifying file system state after copy operations\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The user provided a single massive task description containing: role instructions, repository file list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. This is an automated stitch task from the cobbler pipeline.\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/cp/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 (basic file copy, interactive, force, no-clobber)\n   - Create `cmd/cp/cp_test.go` with differential tests for R1.1-R1.4\n   - Run `go build -o bin/cp ./cmd/cp/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/cp/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/cp/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd056-cp.yaml`) and was about to plan the implementation approach and write the two files (`cmd/cp/main.go` and `cmd/cp/cp_test.go`). No code has been written yet. The task requires implementing a basic `cp` utility with these behaviors:\n   \n   - **R1.1**: `cp SOURCE DEST` copies a single file; `cp SOURCE1 SOURCE2... DEST_DIR` copies multiple files into a directory\n   - **R1.2**: `-i`/`--interactive` prompts on stderr before overwriting, reads y/n from stdin\n   - **R1.3**: `-f`/`--force` removes destination file if can't open for writing, then retries\n   - **R1.4**: `-n`/`--no-clobber` silently skips existing destinations; when combined with `-i`, `-n` takes precedence\n   \n   The implement