{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N2iWeFkvQ5n7ee1gHez36V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Go 1.26.3, so `errors.AsType` is available (added in Go 1.24). And `bytes.SplitSeq` is available too.\n\nLet me fix both issues:\n\n1. In main.go, replace `errors.As` with `errors.AsType`:\n```go\nfunc fmtPathErr(verb, path string, err error) error {\n\tif pe, ok := errors.AsType[*os.PathError](err); ok {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s '%s': %s\", verb, path, pe.Err)\n\n\n```\n\nFinishing the error handling function...\n\nNow for the test file, I need to update the normalization function to use the iterator-based `bytes.SplitSeq` instead of the slice-returning `Split`, iterating through lines with the `range` keyword to filter out lines that don't start with \"try \". I'm realizing there's a subtle issue with how `bytes.SplitSeq` yields subslices — they're views into the original buffer, so I need to be careful about how they're used downstream, especially when appending to the output slice and then joining them back together. `b` won't be garbage collected while `out` holds references to its subslices, and `bytes.Join` creates a fresh copy anyway, so that's safe. I need to verify that `bytes.SplitSeq` is available in Go 1.24 and later, then update the code. For the main.go changes, I'm switching from `errors.As` to `errors.AsType`, which means I can remove the explicit `*os.PathError` variable declaration since the type parameter handles that.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":87314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":343},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"417d3d97-6d07-4097-ab1c-960277983888","uuid":"15b6b